  "description": "Fares, the hourly and daily settlements and the finance report (G1c, ARCHITECTURE decision 36) on the line of boarding.json, on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to g (6656, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e6 f-g, each 1024 long, dead ends at both ends. Alpha (1536, 512), Beta (3584, 512) and Gamma (5632, 512) each have a platform on the half tile of track either side of their node, b, d and f, so a train stops at the node going either way and drives as far from call to call as it did on the grid; Main calls at all three, all day, one train; its round trip takes 14 minutes (sent out at T, Alpha T..T+42 s, then from that departure D: Beta D+2..D+3, Gamma D+5..D+7, Beta D+9..D+10, Alpha D+12), so the line sends Blue out at 1380, 1394, ... (Stage W2b: it boards for at least 42 s and leaves when its doors have closed) Stage W2c (ARCHITECTURE decision 40): Main plans its legs with a crawl, { acceleration 250, braking 250, topSpeed 1 } (1 km/h, about 1024 units a minute): 2048 units take 4 s to reach 1 km/h, 111.2 s at it and 4 s to stop, 119.2, so 120 s, the 2 minutes they took before; the train (standard performance) follows its running curve in the time its timetable gives each leg, so it reaches every call when it did before. Only where it is between calls changes: at the end it is 307 units into e4 going back towards Beta (1331 from f), not 308. Money is in cents. Before any rules a trip pays the flat 5 (500). Distance steps must follow on from 0 without gaps (invalidFareRules); with 0.40 below 40 m and 0.90 beyond, Alpha-Beta (32 m straight) pays 40 and Alpha-Gamma (64 m) 90. Once the company is managed (at 1380) and rules are set, each pair's daily trips are scaled by the fare's demand factor (1037 thousandths at 40, 921 at 90). A passenger pays at boarding, each destination's boarders rounded together to whole dollars: those who board as the doors open, and those who board at each whole minute while they stay open, are each rounded on their own. Every departure of a line's train to its next stop counts with its distance (2048 units a leg). On the hour the hour is settled: operating round(75 departures + 42 train-km + 18 stations), maintenance round(12 route-km + 9 train-km + 8 trains) dollars (3 stations, route 3584 units, 1 train: the line plans its journey from the berth that makes the shortest round trip, the end of Alpha's platform past b going east, 512 units on from b, so its route out is 3584, not 4096; the day's route energy is round(220 x 0.056) = 12 dollars, not 14), with the crowding at that moment; the hour that ends at midnight belongs to the day that ended. At midnight the day's energy round(220 route-km + 360 trains) and staff 620 stations + 480 trains are written, dated 1439, and the balance may go below zero. Every expectation is from the independent G1a/G1b/G1c calculator (GoldenScenarios/README.md).",
